-- title:
--   Existence of a place for a finite separable extension of k(x)
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and $F$ a field equipped with a $k$-algebra structure, and let $x \in F$ be transcendental over $k$. Write $E = k(x)$ for the intermediate field `IntermediateField.adjoin k {x}` of $F/k$ generated by $x$. Assume that $F$ is finite-dimensional as an $E$-vector space and that the extension $F/E$ is separable. The conclusion is that the type [`AlgebraicCurve.Place k F`](def/AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup.html#L22) is nonempty, that is, there exists a valuation subring $\mathcal{O}$ of $F$ such that $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,k\,F\,(a) \in \mathcal{O}$ for every $a \in k$, such that $\mathcal{O} \neq F$ (the subring is not the whole field), and such that $\mathcal{O}$ is a principal ideal ring. Thus a function field $F$ over $k$, presented as a finite separable extension of a rational function field in one transcendental element, carries at least one place in the sense used throughout this development.
--
--   This is the existence of places on an algebraic function field of one variable: every such $F/k$ admits a nontrivial $k$-valuation subring with principal maximal ideal, for instance an extension to $F$ of the $x$-adic valuation of $k(x)$. It serves as the entry point for producing places on the function fields of modular curves, and is used downstream in the work with semistable coverings, integral models and the finite-dimensionality of Riemann–Roch spaces.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_nonempty_place_of_transcendental_of_finiteDimensional.lean

